### Describe the bug

Closing the browser on a long running task does not trigger OnDisconnectedAsync until after the task has finished.
What I'm after is being able to cancel a normal hub method on user disconnect/browser close.


### To Reproduce
``` C#
 public class TestHub : Hub<IProgressHub>
    {

        public override Task OnDisconnectedAsync(Exception exception)
        {
            // This is triggered only after the task has finished.
            return base.OnDisconnectedAsync(exception);
        }


        public async Task<bool> RunTestAsync()
        {
            return (await _TestTaskAsync(this.Context.ConnectionAborted));
        }

        private async Task<bool> _TestTaskAsync(CancellationToken cancel)
        {
            for (int i = 0; i < 1000; i++)
            {
                if (cancel.IsCancellationRequested)
                {
                    // never triggered.
                }

                await Task.Delay(1000);
                await this.Clients.Client(this.Context.ConnectionId).ReportProgress(i.ToString());
            }

            return true;
        }
    }
```

``` C#
 public interface IProgressHub
    {
        Task ReportProgress(string message);
    }
```

