If I run the Task as a stream, cancellation works as expected.
However, this solution is pretty "hacky".

```cs
public async IAsyncEnumerable<bool> RunTestAsync([EnumeratorCancellation]CancellationToken cancelToken)
{
    var result = await _TestTaskAsync(cancelToken);

    yield return result;
}

private async Task<bool> _TestTaskAsync(CancellationToken cancel)
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        if (cancel.IsCancellationRequested)
        {
            // works
        }

        await Task.Delay(1000);
        await this.Clients.Client(this.Context.ConnectionId).ReportProgress(i.ToString());
    }

    return true;
}
```
